  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Don't tell me…?: chẳng lẽ, lẽ nào, không lẽ",
     "texto": [
      "These three open a question that **doesn't really ask**: they show that something seems **unbelievable or unacceptable** to you. They usually end in **sao?**, **à?** or **ư?**:",
      "**Chẳng lẽ** + sentence + **sao / à**? = don't tell me…?, could it be that…?: «**Chẳng lẽ** tôi phải chờ đến chiều **à**?» = Don't tell me I have to wait until the afternoon?",
      "**Không lẽ** is the same, more colloquial (and more southern). **Lẽ nào** is more bookish and more dramatic: «**Lẽ nào** anh ấy quên tôi rồi?» = Could it be that he has already forgotten me?",
      "They also serve to **decide reluctantly**: «**Chẳng lẽ** lại về tay không?» = Are we going to come back empty-handed? (= no, let's do something).",
      "Watch out for «lẽ ra» (should have): they look alike, but don't mean the same."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
